triggers.YaoiHelper/MinimizeGame.placements.name.main=Minimize Game
triggers.YaoiHelper/MinimizeGame.placements.description.main=Minimizes the game.

triggers.YaoiHelper/HDShader.placements.name.main=HD Shader
triggers.YaoiHelper/HDShader.placements.description.main=Applies a high-resolution (1920x1080) shader to the game.\nRequires a HD Shader Controller to function.
triggers.YaoiHelper/HDShader.attributes.description.effects=A comma-seperated list of shaders this trigger should load, relative to Effects and sans file extension.\nIf your shader is in `Effects/mymodname/myshader.cso`, put `mymodname/myshader` here.
triggers.YaoiHelper/HDShader.attributes.description.textures=A list of textures to pass to your shader. Format is <textureslot>:<prefix><identifier>\nThe available prefixes are `%` for mask groups, `$` for GameplayBuffers, `#` for special buffers and `%` for files.\nThe identifier for mask groups is the name of the mask group as defined in the Shader Mask.\nThe identifier for files is the path to the file relative to Graphics/Atlases/Gameplay.
triggers.YaoiHelper/HDShader.attributes.description.flag=If this is populated, the shader will only display when the flag is set.
triggers.YaoiHelper/HDShader.attributes.description.priority=The priority of this trigger's shaders. Higher is later.
triggers.YaoiHelper/HDShader.attributes.description.always_active=Whether the shader should always be active regardless of whether the player is inside it or not.

triggers.YaoiHelper/MouseMovement.placements.name.main=Mouse Control
triggers.YaoiHelper/MouseMovement.placements.description.main=When inside the trigger, teleports Madeline to your mouse every frame.
triggers.YaoiHelper/WindowDance.attributes.description.fling=Whether to fling Madeline when letting go of her. Currently kinda broken
triggers.YaoiHelper/WindowDance.attributes.description.allow_dashing=Whether to disable the teleporting while dashing.
triggers.YaoiHelper/WindowDance.attributes.description.click_and_drag=If enabled, you must put your mouse above Madeline and click to drag her around.
triggers.YaoiHelper/WindowDance.attributes.description.draw_cursor=If enabled, draws a little circle to indicate where your mouse is.

triggers.YaoiHelper/WindowDance.placements.name.main=Window Dance
triggers.YaoiHelper/WindowDance.placements.description.main=Makes the game window move around to follow Madeline.
triggers.YaoiHelper/WindowDance.attributes.description.zoom_level=The amount by which to zoom into the game. This also affects window size

triggers.YaoiHelper/DisableGlitch.placements.name.main=Disable Glitch Effects
triggers.YaoiHelper/DisableGlitch.placements.description.main=Disables the glitch effect without touching the user's photosensitivity setting.

triggers.YaoiHelper/GlobalTimer.placements.name.main=Global Timer
triggers.YaoiHelper/GlobalTimer.placements.description.main=Timer that persists across rooms.
triggers.YaoiHelper/GlobalTimer.attributes.description.ignore_freeze_frames=Whether the timer should run during freeze-frames or not.
triggers.YaoiHelper/GlobalTimer.attributes.description.run_when_paused=Whether the timer should run when the game is paused or not.

triggers.YaoiHelper/PlayerOpacity.placements.name.main=VERY BUGGY Player Opacity

triggers.YaoiHelper/BetterTimerTrigger.placements.name.main=Better Timer
triggers.YaoiHelper/BetterTimerTrigger.placements.description.main='Cause all the other timer triggers suck.
triggers.YaoiHelper/BetterTimerTrigger.attributes.description.time=The amount of time (in seconds) to wait before setting the flag. Ignored if the mode is "Frame count".
triggers.YaoiHelper/BetterTimerTrigger.attributes.description.frames=The amount of frames to wait before setting the flag. Ignored if the mode is not "Frame count".
triggers.YaoiHelper/BetterTimerTrigger.attributes.description.flagToSet=Flag to set once the timer is finished.
triggers.YaoiHelper/BetterTimerTrigger.attributes.description.unsetFlag=Whether to unset the flag instead of setting it when the timer is finished.
triggers.YaoiHelper/BetterTimerTrigger.attributes.description.controlFlag=If non-empty, the timer will only tick down if this flag is set.
triggers.YaoiHelper/BetterTimerTrigger.attributes.description.controlFlagInverted=Invert the requirement for the control flag (if there is one) from set to unset.
triggers.YaoiHelper/BetterTimerTrigger.attributes.description.mode=The mode to use.\nDeltaTime = What you probably want.\nRawDeltaTime = Real-time, ignoring things like modified game speed and freezeframes.\nFrame count = count frames instead of seconds.
triggers.YaoiHelper/BetterTimerTrigger.attributes.description.resetTimerOnLeave=Whether the internal timer should be reset when the player leaves the trigger.
triggers.YaoiHelper/BetterTimerTrigger.attributes.description.resetTimerOnControlFlagUnset=Whether the internal timer should be reset EVERY FRAME while the control flag isn't set (affected as one would expect by Control Flag Inverted).
triggers.YaoiHelper/BetterTimerTrigger.attributes.description.unsetOnRoomLoad=Whether the Flag To Set should be unset (or set if Unset Flag is enabled) on room load.
triggers.YaoiHelper/BetterTimerTrigger.attributes.name.compareLOnly=Compare With >
triggers.YaoiHelper/BetterTimerTrigger.attributes.description.compareLOnly=Whether the comparison should be (timer > time) instead of (timer >= time), meaning the internal timer must be larger than the time specified to activate.\nProbably not very useful unless you're using the frame count mode.

triggers.YaoiHelper/ForceInputsTrigger.placements.name.main=Force Inputs
triggers.YaoiHelper/ForceInputsTrigger.placements.description.main=A barebones Celeste interface that allows you to force certain inputs to be pressed/released from the "point of view" of `Player.Update()`.
triggers.YaoiHelper/ForceInputsTrigger.attributes.description.inputs=List of comma-separated inputs, formatted similarly to a TAS (e.g "R,U,X"). An input can be prefixed with ! to force releasing it.\nSupported inputs: LRUDJXZG (in TAS format).
triggers.YaoiHelper/ForceInputsTrigger.attributes.description.flag=If non-empty, the trigger will only be active when this flag is set.
triggers.YaoiHelper/ForceInputsTrigger.attributes.description.flagInverted=Invert the requirement for the flag (if there is one) from set to unset.
triggers.YaoiHelper/ForceInputsTrigger.attributes.description.showStatus=Whether status text at the bottom-left corner of the screen should be shown while the player is inside the trigger.
triggers.YaoiHelper/ForceInputsTrigger.attributes.description.statusPrefix=What to display in the status alongside the inputs.
triggers.YaoiHelper/ForceInputsTrigger.attributes.description.hideStatusInCutscenes=Use with Show Status - whether the status should be hidden while in a cutscene / bino.
triggers.YaoiHelper/ForceInputsTrigger.attributes.description.extraStatusVerticalPadding=Extra distance for the status text from the bottom of the screen in pixels.

triggers.YaoiHelper/NonBrokenInstantCameraCatchupTrigger.placements.name.main=Non-Broken Instant Camera Catchup
triggers.YaoiHelper/NonBrokenInstantCameraCatchupTrigger.placements.description.main=So VivHelper's Instant Camera Catchup trigger is broken because it does this thing where the camera remains locked onto you until OnLeave is called.\nSo if something happens that causes it to not get called (say, teleporting with debug map, save & quit, etc.), the camera will stay locked onto you for the rest of the session (unless you enter and leave another Instant Camera Catchup trigger).\nThis fixes that by either:\n- Making the camera lock expire after 1 frame (even if you stay inside the trigger), so it actually works like "just catch up the camera" like you probably thought it already did.\n- If you actually do want the camera to stay locked onto the player, you can untoggle Only On Enter. This still has fixes over VivHelper; leaving the room by means like debug map or save and quit properly unlocks the camera.
triggers.YaoiHelper/NonBrokenInstantCameraCatchupTrigger.attributes.description.flag=If non-empty, the trigger will only work when this flag is set.
triggers.YaoiHelper/NonBrokenInstantCameraCatchupTrigger.attributes.description.flagInverted=Invert the requirement for the flag (if there is one) from set to unset.
triggers.YaoiHelper/NonBrokenInstantCameraCatchupTrigger.attributes.description.onlyOnEnter=Whether the camera should simply snap to the player when the trigger is entered and do nothing else.\nIf unchecked, it'll keep following the player while it's inside the trigger.

triggers.YaoiHelper/ShowStatusTrigger.placements.name.main=Show Status
triggers.YaoiHelper/ShowStatusTrigger.placements.description.main=Displays a piece of text in the bottom left corner on the screen.
triggers.YaoiHelper/ShowStatusTrigger.attributes.description.text=Text to display. Allows colors, e.g `{#ff0000}red text` or `{00ff00}green{#}normal`.
triggers.YaoiHelper/ShowStatusTrigger.attributes.description.hideInCutscenes=Whether the text should be hidden while in a cutscene / bino.
triggers.YaoiHelper/ShowStatusTrigger.attributes.description.extraVerticalPadding=Extra distance from the bottom of the screen in pixels.
triggers.YaoiHelper/ShowStatusTrigger.attributes.description.instantRender=Use a slightly more expensive approach to render/unrender on the same frame the player enters/leaves the trigger, instead of up to 1f late on entry and up to 2f late on exit.

triggers.YaoiHelper/SpeedFadeTrigger.placements.name.main=Speed Fade Trigger
triggers.YaoiHelper/SpeedFadeTrigger.placements.description.main=Fades the trigger under the node based on the speed of the player.
triggers.YaoiHelper/SpeedFadeTrigger.attributes.description.lower_bound=Speed values below this get clamped to 0%.
triggers.YaoiHelper/SpeedFadeTrigger.attributes.description.upper_bound=Speed values above this get clamped to 100%.


entities.YaoiHelper/HDShaderController.placements.name.main=HD Shader Controller
entities.YaoiHelper/HDShaderController.placements.description.main=Adjusts the behavior of HD Shader triggers.\nRequired for said triggers to function.
entities.YaoiHelper/HDShaderController.attributes.description.render_player_over=If enabled, renders the player over the active shaders (and also some other things, such as darkness alpha)
entities.YaoiHelper/HDShaderController.attributes.description.render_level_over=If enabled, renders the level over the active shaders, although without stylegrounds.

entities.YaoiHelper/BuildController.placements.name.main=Build Controller
entities.YaoiHelper/BuildController.placements.description.main=Allows the player to build and mine tiles.
entities.YaoiHelper/BuildController.attributes.description.unlimited=Whether the amount of tiles should be unlimited or not.
entities.YaoiHelper/BuildController.attributes.description.tile_limit=If not unlimited, the amount of tiles the player should have for the current room.

